## Bug Council Audit Complete

**PR:** https://github.com/Coconut-Banking/coconut-app/pull/39

### Summary

| Phase | Result |
|-------|--------|
| Agents deployed | 7 (NAV, AUTH, PAYMENTS, API, NATIVE, UISTATE, FLOWS) |
| Bugs found | 35 (before dedup) → 30 unique |
| Bugs fixed | **28** |
| Bugs deferred | 2 (product-decision) |
| New TS errors introduced | 0 |

### Fixed by Severity

**P0 — Critical (3)**
- Hardcoded Clerk publishable key in source
- Auth token not checked before Stripe Terminal connection fetch (empty `Authorization` header)
- User email leaked via `console.log` on every sign-in

**P1 — Broken Functionality (10)**
- `FORCE_SIGN_OUT_ON_LAUNCH` permanently disabled token cache
- `connected` deep link unreachable when app is unauthenticated on cold launch
- Sign-out navigation race (`router.replace` vs `AuthSwitch` re-render)
- Payment amount sent in dollars instead of cents to Stripe
- Android permissions array excluded Stripe Terminal's required location/Bluetooth perms
- `res.json()` called before `res.ok` check in two fetch paths
- `linked` state never reset after bank disconnection
- Receipt confirm errors silently swallowed

**P2 — Incorrect Behavior (15)**
- SafeAreaView missing from 5 screens (insights, pay, sign-in, sign-up, shared person-detail)
- Insights showed "Connect your bank" wall during loading for linked users
- `AbortController` timeout didn't cover the `/api/plaid/transactions` fetch
- Plus 8 more navigation, state, and UX correctness fixes

**Deferred (need product decision)**
- Pay tab directly accessible from tab bar with no amount/group params
- `TerminalTokenProvider` mounted in `SKIP_AUTH` demo mode
